    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d529">

                <pb facs="0576" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg566"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/10936: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-12T19:00:00-04:00">June 12, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1479. Reference your 1920, May 29, 5 p.m., and 2003, June 5, noon,<anchor n="78"
                        xml:id="d529-f1"/> Department has not received any confirmation from
                    Stockholm that Johnson and Griffis gave Madame Kollontay assurance quoted in
                    Molotov’s note of May 28.<anchor n="79" xml:id="d529-f2"/> As it appears that no
                    general embargo will be placed on the export of ball bearings from Sweden for
                    the time <pb facs="0577" n="567" xml:id="pg567"/> being the matter is not of
                    immediate importance. However, the Legation at Stockholm has been requested to
                    report regarding their conversation of May 17 with Madame Kollontay and further
                    instructions will then be sent to the Embassy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d529-f1" n="78" xml:id="d529-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d529-f2" n="79" xml:id="d529-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram 1920, May 29. 5 p.m., <ref target="#pg557">p. 557</ref>.</p>
